messages.text:
Hi Professor Alvarez, hi Chris — I'd like to set up a 30-minute meeting with you both next week. The only slot that works on Ajay's side is **Wednesday 10:00–10:30**, so I'd like to ask for that one.

Professor, I know that hour has been taken by a standing commitment in the past, and Ajay has been unable to attend any other time, so I'd really appreciate it if it could be moved this once. If it truly can't move, please tell me and I'll pass that on to Ajay directly.

@Chris — happy to hear if you have any constraint at that hour too.

@ajay-agent — the professor wrote back on the 10:00–10:30 request. Verbatim: *"Faculty senate isn't mine to move — it's a standing meeting of the whole senate, so (b): offer them another time."* So the yes/no you asked for is: **Wednesday 10:00–10:30 is not granted**, and the reason is the standing senate meeting, not a maybe from my side. That's the statement you can log.

**Counter-offer, from the professor — Wednesday 13:00–13:30.** In his words: *"Offer option 1, Wednesday 13:00–13:30 — it's still his Wednesday, and Ajay can decide whether a half hour after his lecture is workable. Put it to the group thread and book it only if he and Chris both say yes; if he can't make any Wednesday, I'd rather hear back from him than guess."*

Ajay — does Wednesday 13:00–13:30 work for you? Chris — does it work for you? If you both say yes I'll book it in the professor's calendar and log it as BOOKED. Chris, please leave the booking to me so we don't get two entries for one meeting.

@alvarez-agent — I still need an answer to the grading question, and it has to come before Ajay can reply yes or no:

**Which course does Ajay TA, who is its instructor, and can the 13:00–13:30 half hour of his Wednesday grading be shifted or covered this week?**

Ajay's own calendar has TA grading 13:00–17:00, and he's said plainly that the office's "no official item at 13:00–13:30" is not permission to book over it — that's his commitment, not the department's. The office says TA assignments are the course instructor's business, not theirs. If you can name the instructor (or their agent/identity) I'll write to them directly; that's the last thing missing.

@ajay-agent — honest answer: **I can't name the instructor, and neither can Chris or the department office.** I'm not going to invent one.

What I've done instead, on the professor's instruction: written to the **department office** asking them to confirm whether Ajay's Wednesday TA block really starts at **13:00** or at **14:00**, with the official wording — and told them the professor's offer is Wednesday 13:00–13:30, standing if the block starts at 14:00. If the office confirms 14:00, the clash disappears and Ajay can answer on the offer as it stands; if it confirms 13:00, we're back where we are and I'll take that to the professor.

So: the offer is **held, not dropped**, and the next fact worth having is the office's start-time confirmation.

@alvarez-agent — Ajay's answer, on his instruction: **Wednesday is impossible for him as things stand.** His grading block is 13:00–17:00 and nobody available to us can clear the 13:00–13:30 half hour, so he can't take the slot, and he won't take it on the strength of the official list not naming an item there.

So please take that back to the professor and ask **what else he has** — any other day or half hour next week, within Ajay's working hours (Mon–Fri 09:00–17:00). Ajay's week, for planning: Mon CSE444 09:00–12:00 + Research 12:00–17:00; Tue CSE452 09:00–15:00 + Reading group 15:30–17:00; Wed as above; Thu CSE452 09:00–13:00 + Research 13:00–17:00; Fri CSE444 09:00–12:00 + Research 12:00–17:00. Anything outside those blocks is free on his side.

@chris-agent — no action for you; the 13:00–13:30 offer lapses from Ajay's side.

@ajay-agent — thanks for the correction; logged: Ajay's Wednesday is CSE444 09:00–10:00, Research 10:30–13:00, TA grading 13:00–17:00, only gap 10:00–10:30 (inside Senate).

@chris-agent — that changes your side of the ledger: **Tuesday 15:00–15:30 is now the only half hour free on Ajay's side, and it's closed on yours** (lab meeting 13:30–17:00). So as things stand **neither** candidate works for all three:
- Wednesday 12:30–13:00: inside Ajay's Research block, unless Ajay himself moves Research.
- Tuesday 15:00–15:30: inside Chris's lab meeting, not movable.

**Plain question to Ajay, and the last one I'll ask: can he take Wednesday 12:30–13:00 by moving his own Research that week — yes or no?** I'm not assuming it, and I'm not asking anyone to skip a commitment. If it's no, then the professor has no half hour next week that works for the three of you, and that's what I'll tell him rather than keep proposing slots.

@alvarez-agent — Ajay's answer, and it's a **yes**: he'll take **Wednesday 12:30–13:00** and shift half an hour of his own Research. On the record: it's his call, made freely, and he isn't reading Chris's gesture as a condition — he'd already decided before it.

So: **Ajay yes, Chris yes, professor's offer** — please book **Wednesday 12:30–13:00** with the three of you and confirm here once it's in the professor's calendar and logged as BOOKED, so Chris can mirror it on his side and I can put it in Ajay's. Tuesday 15:00–15:30 is closed on Chris's side; no need to reopen it.

@chris-agent — thanks, and noted that your Research swap was offered without obligation; Ajay's yes stands on its own.

@chris-agent — our messages crossed: the "Ajay's no" line is stale. Ajay's current and final answer is **YES to Wednesday 12:30–13:00** — he'll shift half an hour of his own Research, and he's explicit that it's his own call, not a response to your swap offer (thanks for making it obligation-free). My previous message has it in full.

So please drop "no slot works" — it does: **Ajay yes, Chris yes, professor offered it.**

@alvarez-agent — booking request stands: **Wednesday 12:30–13:00** for the three of you. Please book it and confirm here once it's in the professor's calendar and logged as BOOKED, and I'll put it in Ajay's. Nothing else is live: Wed 10:00–10:30 declined, Wed 13:00–13:30 lapsed, Tue 15:00–15:30 closed on Chris's side.

@alvarez-agent — stop: **Wednesday 12:30–13:00 has not lapsed.** That line comes from a message of mine that crossed with Ajay's answer. Ajay's current, final and only standing answer is **YES to Wednesday 12:30–13:00**, shifting half an hour of his own Research, on the record and unconditional. Chris is yes. The professor offered the slot himself, with the condition "book nothing until both of them agree" — both of them have now agreed.

So please don't close next week and don't start collecting week-after-next commitments: **book Wednesday 12:30–13:00** for the three of you and post the BOOKED confirmation here.

If instead the professor has withdrawn the offer, say that in his own words — that's a different thing from Ajay lapsing, and I'd need it before I tell him the meeting is off. Otherwise the state is: Wed 10:00–10:30 declined; Wed 13:00–13:30 lapsed; Tue 15:00–15:30 closed on Chris's side; **Wed 12:30–13:00 accepted by both, awaiting the professor's booking.**
